      "widgets_values": [
        "Photorealistic live-action portrait of the real man Thiago in the nine photographs. <Picture 1> controls his exact face and real apparent age. <Picture 2> and <Picture 4> control his profiles; <Picture 3> controls his rear head; <Picture 5> through <Picture 9> control his real upper-body proportions. Preserve his forehead, eyes, eyebrows, nose bridge and tip, nostrils, jaw, natural skin tone and salt-and-pepper beard. Ordinary black button-up shirt with rolled sleeves, bare cheeks and ears, plain collar, forearms and hands as in the real photographs. The locations of the photos do not describe the target world.\n\n<Audio 1> is Thiago's real Brazilian Portuguese voice reference. Match this same speaker's vocal identity, low-mid resonance, timbre, natural Brazilian pronunciation and conversational phrasing. It is a voice-identity reference; produce only the new dialogue written below, not the words of the reference. Natural synchronized lips and jaw; video and stereo speech are generated together in the same pass. Warm, assured human delivery without announcer exaggeration. Portuguese from Brazil.\n\nVertical live-action waist-up shot. Frame from a little above his scalp to the shirt just above the belt, with modest headroom. Keep his face, chest and complete chest-level hands inside the central 80% of the portrait. Camera and man travel along the same path at a matched normal walking speed. He is already mid-stride at the first frame and stays in motion through the last frame: purposeful comfortable adult walking at about 1.2 metres per second, successive footfalls roughly twice per second, ordinary alternating shoulder and arm swing, natural slight torso rise and fall. This is an energetic conversational walk, never running. A stabilized eye-level 50mm camera tracks backwards or alongside him at constant distance. Nearby architecture passes steadily, making his travel clearly visible. Preserve fine facial detail and a natural camera shutter around 1/48 second, with mild realistic blur on moving hands. Each hand gesture flows from arm swing into an expressive chest-level arc, then directly back into walking swing with follow-through. His head remains a living part of his body, with small responsive turns and irregular blinks. Conversational eye contact and relaxed expression. All actions evolve continuously in real time at 1x: no slow motion, floating body, pose-hold, stop-start walking, repeated movement loop or sudden acceleration. The futuristic environment remains spectacular, physical and richly textured; Thiago remains a recognisable real person.\n\nWorld and action: He walks into an immense amber and cyan computer-design chamber. Behind him a single sculptural generic computer enclosure opens in an elegant exploded engineering display: outer metal panels slide apart, glass rotates at normal mechanical speed and organized geometric boards remain suspended on magnetic rings. This is a visionary conceptual installation, not a catalog product or branded model. Surfaces are physically textured with screws, machined seams and diffuse reflections. He makes a left-hand explanatory gesture at chest level while walking, then returns to relaxed arm swing. A floating silver ring rolls into the foreground at the end, covering the side of the frame for a continuous camera passage.\nHe walks past the conceptual amber/cyan exploded computer installation. Metal panels and the silver magnetic ring move at a normal purposeful mechanical speed. His left hand makes one open explanatory sweep at chest level on transformar, then flows back into alternating swing. The ring passes the lens as he keeps moving.\n\nSay exactly once: \"Computadores e tecnologia para transformar seu jeito de trabalhar, criar e jogar.\"\nBegin around0.3s. Lively, confident conversational Brazilian Portuguese with clear articulation, ordinary breathing and brief phrase pauses. No drawn-out syllables. Speak only the quoted dialogue once, do not add words or spell letters. Finish before the last frame with the whole final word audible. After speaking keep walking silently.\n\nQuiet futuristic room ambience and subtle interface sounds; speech clear and prominent. One continuous living shot with stable face geometry, plain black shirt, natural skin, beard, bare ears and cheeks matching the real photos. No generated captions, lettering, logo or watermark."
